module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.refusal_deferred_to_emitted_runtime

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data refusal_deferred_to_emitted_runtime: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "refusal_deferred_to_emitted_runtime" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "refusal deferred to the emitted runtime (a compiler refusal expressed as a construct IN THE EMITTED PROGRAM rather than as a diagnostic in the COMPILING one, so the compile reports success and the line does not stop). ",

    "INVALID STATE: an emission path that cannot answer a declared fact writes a panic, an error expression or a stub into the artifact and returns normally, so the compiler emits N files and reports zero diagnostics beside a body that cannot run. ",

    "HARM: fabricated plausible output at the strongest grain -- an artifact that looks like a compiled program and is not one. ",

    "The refusal message may be perfectly honest and still fail DESIGN section 5, because nobody reads it until production; the reviewer's three questions are does the line stop, is the stop typed and located, does analysis precede restart, and this arm fails the first. ",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the tell is a SUCCESS REPORT beside a refusal construct in the same run -- 'compiled: 7 files emitted, 0 diagnostics' printed by a compile whose emitted body was a panic naming its own refusal. ",

    "It is NOT the same as a legitimate runtime arm at an honest boundary: the discriminator is whether the compiler KNEW at emit time, from modeled structure, that the artifact could not answer. ",

    "If it knew and wrote the knowledge into the output instead of the diagnostic stream, the class applies. ",

    "SPECIMEN AND HOW IT WAS FOUND: gunbc#9886's shell service-emission climb refused an unrealizable output channel by emitting panic!() from emit_shell_channel_expr while emit_artifact returned its files normally. ",

    "Found by a DIFFERENTIAL READ against an independent implementation of the same repair (calm-boar-314's superseded WIP), then by execution on a probe; five consecutive reviews APPROVED the arm, two of them praising the refusal by name, so review did not catch it and is not the mechanism that will. ",

    "WHY REVIEW MISSES IT: the refusal is present, typed, located and honestly worded at the point a reader's eye lands, and the missing half is an ABSENCE elsewhere -- no diagnostic in a stream the diff does not show. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: for every arm that emits a refusal construct into a target artifact, ask what the COMPILE reports on the same input. ",

    "If the answer is success, or any file count above zero, the arm belongs to this class. ",

    "REPAIR, and it is usually already written next door: pair the refusal expression with a blocking emit-stage diagnostic so the artifact producer returns no files. ",

    "In the specimen the FILE transport already had that pair and shell had the expression half only, so the repair was building the twin rather than inventing a path -- which is the general shape, since a codebase that emits refusals at all usually has one arm that does it correctly. ",

    "KEEP THE EXPRESSION as the unreachable second half rather than deleting it, so the two readers cannot disagree if the wall is ever weakened. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable -- a runtime panic in generated code, established by executing the emitter and reading its own success line, NOT by reading the type. ",

    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed, and reached in the specimen -- a located compile-time refusal per declared field, derived from modeled structure, with zero files emitted. ",

    "NEXT TRIGGER for the class as a whole: an emission-stage census that pairs every refusal-construct emitter with its diagnostic twin, since nothing today makes the missing half visible and the specimen was found by accident. ",

    "POPULATION NOTE THE SPECIMEN CARRIES: the wall converted a SILENT corpus defect into a loud one -- gunbc.WitnessBin.Run declares stderr_truncated, stderr_total_bytes and stderr_retained_bytes, three channels the Rust realization cannot answer because the emitted Command body implements no capture policy, so every entry closure reaching that operation now refuses at field grain. ",

    "That was always true and the old arm said nothing. ",

    "Measured OUTSIDE REQUIRED COVERAGE, which is the honest phrasing and not 'affects nothing': claim_executor --required-emit-compile is green on all 8 rostered entries, each with its own mutation-established red, those 8 reaching 47 modules, with ZERO shell-channel diagnostics.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
